# Drizzle ORM + Neon

This project uses **Drizzle ORM** connected to a **Neon serverless Postgres** database. Never use raw SQL or other ORM libraries.

## Key Files

- `src/db/index.ts` — Drizzle client (import `db` from here)
- `src/db/schema.ts` — all table definitions
- `drizzle.config.ts` — Drizzle Kit configuration
- `.env` — contains `DATABASE_URL` (Neon connection string)

## Using the Database

```typescript
import db from "@/db"
import { usersTable } from "@/db/schema"
import { eq } from "drizzle-orm"

// Select
const users = await db.select().from(usersTable)

// Insert
await db.insert(usersTable).values({ name: "Alice", age: 30, email: "alice@example.com" })

// Update
await db.update(usersTable).set({ age: 31 }).where(eq(usersTable.email, "alice@example.com"))

// Delete
await db.delete(usersTable).where(eq(usersTable.email, "alice@example.com"))
```

## Schema Changes

1. Edit `src/db/schema.ts`
2. Push changes: `npx drizzle-kit push`
   — or generate + apply migrations: `npx drizzle-kit generate` then `npx drizzle-kit migrate`

## Rules

- All table definitions go in `src/db/schema.ts`
- Always use Drizzle query builder — never raw SQL strings
- Use `process.env.DATABASE_URL` only via the centralised client in `src/db/index.ts`
